{
    "title": "Expect multicolumn values to be equal",
    "description": "Expect the values in each row of the specified columns to be equal.\n\nExpectMulticolumnValuesToBeEqual is a Multicolumn Map Expectation.\n\nMulticolumn Map Expectations evaluate a set of columns row by row and calculate the\npercentage of rows that meet the condition. Nulls compare safely: a row of null values\nis equal, while a null and a non-null value are not equal.\n\nArgs:\n    column_list (tuple or list): Set of columns to be checked.\n\nOther Parameters:\n    ignore_row_if (str): If specified, sets the condition on which a given row is to be ignored. Default \"never\".\n    mostly (None or a float between 0 and 1): Successful if at least `mostly` fraction of values match the Expectation.\n    result_format (str or None): Which output mode to use: BOOLEAN_ONLY, BASIC,\n        COMPLETE, or SUMMARY.\n    catch_exceptions (boolean or None): If True, include exceptions in the result.\n    meta (dict or None): A JSON-serializable dictionary included in the output.\n    severity (str or None): The impact of this Expectation failing: critical, warning, or info. Defaults to critical if not set. Severity levels can be used to trigger different alerting patterns and actions.\n\nReturns:\n    An [ExpectationSuiteValidationResult](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/terms/validation_result)\n\nSupported Data Sources:\n    [Pandas](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [Spark](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [SQLite](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [PostgreSQL](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [Citus](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [AlloyDB](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [Neon](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [MySQL](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [SQL Server](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [BigQuery](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [Snowflake](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [Databricks (SQL)](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n    [Redshift](https://docs.greatexpectations.io/docs/application_integration_support/)\n\nData Quality Issues:\n    Validity\n\nExample Data:\n        source  copy  archive\n    0   A       A     A\n    1   B       B     C\n    2   null    null  null\n\nCode Examples:\n    Passing Case:\n        ExpectMulticolumnValuesToBeEqual(\n            column_list=[\"source\", \"copy\", \"archive\"], mostly=0.66\n        )\n\n    Failing Case:\n        ExpectMulticolumnValuesToBeEqual(\n            column_list=[\"source\", \"copy\", \"archive\"]\n        )",
